      "output": {
        "decision": "answer",
        "reason": "The evidence explicitly and consistently states the dataset is automatically generated without human labeling. The Abstract says they 'propose a method to automatically generate labeled datasets for NER'; the Introduction says they 'construct labeled datasets without human supervision' and call it 'weakly-supervised' (silver standard); the Conclusion states they 'presented a method to generate a massively-sized labeled dataset for NER in an automatic fashion, without human labor involved in labeling.' Thus the corpus (SESAME) is completely automatically generated, though it is a silver-standard rather than gold-standard corpus."
      },
      "elapsed_ms": 4778.434899984859
    },
